{"step_index":864,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-02T18:04:42Z","input_tokens":2640,"cache_read_tokens":43890,"output_tokens":1385,"content":"### Table Column Alignment & Post-Processing Swap Fix Completed\n\nThe invoice parser has been updated across both the **FastAPI Python backend** and the **JavaScript client engine** to resolve column alignment issues and prevent quantity/rate swaps.\n\n---\n\n### Key Implementations\n\n#### 1. Gemini Extraction Prompt Updated\nAdded table-parsing and column-boundary alignment rules to `TABLE COLUMN ALIGNMENT INSTRUCTIONS` in [server.py](file:///Users/pranit405/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/audit-it/server.py#L102-L107) and [utils/aiExtractor.js](file:///Users/pranit405/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/audit-it/utils/aiExtractor.js#L20-L29):\n- **Column Boundaries:** Locates column headers (`S.No`, `Description`, `HSN/SAC`, `Quantity`, `Unit`, `Rate/Price`, `Amount`).\n- **Internal Cross-Checking:** Verifies that $\\text{quantity} \\times \\text{unit\\_rate} \\approx \\text{total\\_amount}$. Warns against mistaking S.No/HSN/Code for Quantity.\n- **Trivial Rate Prevention:** Forbids assigning rate `1` or `2` to expensive equipment (e.g. `Tool Kit`).\n- **Unit Stripping:** Trims packaging abbreviations like `NO`, `NOS`, `PCS`, `PKT`, `SET` from product descriptions.\n\n#### 2. Post-Processing Column Swap Fallback\nImplemented the column swap check and unit sanitizer across backend and frontend layers:\n- [server.py](file:///Users/pranit405/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/audit-it/server.py#L134-L148):\n  ```python\n  for item in items:\n      qty = item.get('quantity', 0)\n      rate = item.get('unit_rate', 0)\n      total = item.get('total_amount', 0)\n      \n      # If total matches qty exactly and rate is small (e.g. qty=535, rate=2, total=535), \n      # it means qty and rate were misaligned. Swap them:\n      if total > 0 and qty == total and rate in [1, 2, 1.0, 2.0]:\n          item['quantity'] = 1.0\n          item['unit_rate'] = total\n  ```\n- [utils/clean_items.py](file:///Users/pranit405/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/audit-it/utils/clean_items.py#L61-L71): Applied in `clean_extracted_items()` and `sanitize_invoice_data()`.\n- [utils/itemCleaner.js](file:///Users/pranit405/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/audit-it/utils/itemCleaner.js#L64-L71) & [utils/privacyMasker.js](file:///Users/pranit405/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/audit-it/utils/privacyMasker.js#L94-L99): Matches client-side parsing pipeline.\n\n---\n\n### Verification Results\n\nA unit test was executed against the API with an inverted input:\n```json\n{\n  \"description\": \"Heavy Duty Tool Kit NOS\",\n  \"quantity\": 535,\n  \"unit_rate\": 2,\n  \"total_amount\": 535.0\n}\n```\n\n**Normalized Output:**\n- `description`: `\"Heavy Duty Tool Kit\"` (trailing unit `NOS` trimmed)\n- `quantity`: `1.0`\n- `unit_rate`: `535.0`\n- `total_amount`: `535.0`\n\nThe FastAPI server is active and serving the application at `http://localhost:3000`.","thinking":"All user instructions have been implemented and verified. The final response will detail the table column alignment instructions integrated into both the backend (Python) and frontend (JavaScript) extraction processes.\n\n\n"}
{"step_index":865,"source":"USER_EXPLICIT","type":"USER_INPUT","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-02T18:12:05Z","content":"<USER_REQUEST>\nCRITICAL FIX FOR INVOICE EXTRACTION & MATH AUDIT ENGINE:\n\nFix the OCR parsing, comma handling, garbage line-item filtering, and grand total extraction across the backend:\n\n1. UPDATE THE GEMINI EXTRACTION PROMPT:\nReplace the system prompt with these strict rules:\n\n\"You are an Indian GST Tax Invoice extractor. Your job is to extract exact numbers and text without dropping digits or inventing items.\n\nCRITICAL RULES:\n1. COMMA & NUMBER HANDLING (DO NOT DROP DIGITS):\n   - In Indian currency notation, commas are thousands separators. NEVER drop digits before commas!\n   - Example: '2,535.00' is 2535.0 (Two Thousand Five Hundred Thirty-Five), NOT 535.\n   - Example: '1,270.00' is 1270.0 (One Thousand Two Hundred Seventy), NOT 270.\n   - Always verify extracted figures against the printed 'Amount/Total in Words' (e.g., 'FOUR THOUSAND FOUR HUNDRED AND NINETY RUPEES ONLY' means the total is 4490, not 2173).\n\n2. ONLY REAL PRODUCTS/SERVICES IN LINE ITEMS:\n   - Extract ONLY genuine products or services from the central invoice table (e.g., 'Bosch All-in-One Metal Hand Tool Kit', 'Taparia Universal Tool Kit').\n   - Clean the product description: strip table borders, brackets, or leading/trailing symbols like '[', '|', ']', or unit words like 'NOS'/'PCS'.\n   - NEVER extract rubber stamps, signatures, authorization seals, or hand scribbles (e.g., symbols like '©', '~', '|', '[', ']').\n\n3. GRAND TOTAL EXTRACTION:\n   - Look strictly for the final 'Grand Total', 'Total Amount', 'Net Payable', or 'कुल योग' at the bottom of the invoice (e.g., 4,490.00).\n   - DO NOT hallucinate the grand total by summing OCR misreads. Extract the actual printed total on the invoice.\n\n4. COLUMN INTEGRITY:\n   - Quantity is typically an integer (e.g., 1, 2, 5).\n   - Rate is the unit price (e.g., 2535.00, 1270.00).\n   - Billed Amount must reflect (Quantity * Unit Rate).\"\n\n2. BACKEND POST-PROCESSING & SANITIZATION (Python):\nAdd/update this cleaning function to run on the extracted JSON before sending it to the frontend:\n\nimport re\n\ndef sanitize_and_clean_invoice(data: dict) -> dict:\n    # 1. Clean supplier name of trailing symbols\n    if data.get(\"vendor_name\"):\n        data[\"vendor_name\"] = re.sub(r'[\\s&0\\|\\[\\]\\(\\)]+$', '', data[\"vendor_name\"]).strip()\n\n    # 2. Filter garbage line items\n    clean_items = []\n    for item in data.get(\"items\", []):\n        desc = (item.get(\"description\") or \"\").strip()\n        \n        # Remove stray leading/trailing brackets and vertical pipes from OCR\n        desc = re.sub(r'^[\\[\\|\\]\\(\\)\\s]+|[\\[\\|\\]\\(\\)\\s]+$', '', desc).strip()\n        item[\"description\"] = desc\n\n        # Skip if description lacks at least 4 letters\n        if len(re.findall(r'[a-zA-Z]', desc)) < 4:\n            continue\n\n        # Skip if more than 20% of description is weird symbols/punctuation\n        symbols = re.findall(r'[~|©\\[\\]=_{}@#$%^&*]', desc)\n        if len(desc) > 0 and (len(symbols) / len(desc)) > 0.20:\n            continue\n\n        # Skip common footer/stamp terms\n        if any(term in desc.lower() for term in [\"signature\", \"authorised\", \"terms\", \"condition\", \"bank details\"]):\n            continue\n\n        # Quantity and Rate sanity\n        qty = float(item.get(\"quantity\") or 1)\n        rate = float(str(item.get(\"unit_rate\") or 0).replace(\",\", \"\"))\n        billed = float(str(item.get(\"total_amount\") or (qty * rate)).replace(\",\", \"\"))\n\n        item[\"quantity\"] = qty\n        item[\"unit_rate\"] = rate\n        item[\"total_amount\"] = billed\n        clean_items.append(item)\n\n    data[\"items\"] = clean_items\n\n    # 3. Ensure numeric fields strip commas cleanly\n    for key in [\"subtotal\", \"cgst\", \"sgst\", \"igst\", \"declared_total\"]:\n        if data.get(key) is not None:\n            data[key] = float(str(data[key]).replace(\",\", \"\").strip())\n\n    return data\n\nApply `sanitize_and_clean_invoice` to all Gemini outputs before updating the UI state.\n</USER_REQUEST>\n<ADDITIONAL_METADATA>\nThe current local time is: 2026-11-02T23:42:05+05:30.\n</ADDITIONAL_METADATA>"}
