{"step_index":899,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-02T18:14:17Z","content":"Created At: 2026-11-02T23:44:17+05:30\nCompleted At: 2026-11-02T23:44:17+05:30\nShowing lines 88-160 of 211\n88:     \n89:     # Prompt with table column alignment instructions\n90:     prompt = \"\"\"Extract the invoice details from this image/document into JSON:\n91:  - vendor_name: (string)\n92:  - gstin: (string or null)\n93:  - invoice_number: (string or null)\n94:  - items: list of {description, quantity, unit_rate, total_amount}\n95:  - subtotal: (number)\n96:  - cgst: (number)\n97:  - sgst: (number)\n98:  - igst: (number)\n99:  - declared_total: (number)\n100:  If any field is missing or unclear, leave it null. Do not include addresses or phone numbers as line items.\n101: \n102: TABLE COLUMN ALIGNMENT INSTRUCTIONS:\n103: - Carefully identify the table header row to locate column boundaries (S.No, Description, HSN/SAC, Quantity, Unit, Rate/Price, Amount).\n104: - CROSS-CHECK MATH INTERNALLY: For each row, verify that (quantity * unit_rate) roughly equals the row total amount. \n105:   * If quantity * rate does not equal the row amount, you likely swapped the Quantity and Rate columns, or confused the Item Code/HSN/S.No with Quantity. \n106:   * Never set Rate to trivial numbers like 1 or 2 when the item is an expensive product like a 'Tool Kit', unless that is explicitly the printed unit rate.\n107: - Clean description: Do not append units like 'NO', 'PCS', 'NOS', or serial numbers into the product description.\"\"\"\n108: \n109:     genai_client = get_genai_client(x_api_key)\n110:     if not genai_client:\n111:         return JSONResponse(\n112:             status_code=400,\n113:             content={\"error\": \"Gemini API key is required.\"}\n114:         )\n115: \n116:     # Call Gemini (primary: gemini-2.5-flash; fallback to gemini-3.5-flash if 404/unavailable)\n117:     models_to_try = ['gemini-2.5-flash', 'gemini-3.5-flash', 'gemini-3.8-flash']\n118:     last_err = None\n119: \n120:     for model_name in models_to_try:\n121:         try:\n122:             response = genai_client.models.generate_content(\n123:                 model=model_name,\n124:                 contents=[\n125:                     types.Part.from_bytes(data=contents, mime_type=mime_type),\n126:                     prompt\n127:                 ],\n128:                 config=types.GenerateContentConfig(\n129:                     response_mime_type=\"application/json\",\n130:                     response_schema=ExtractedInvoice,\n131:                     temperature=0.0\n132:                 )\n133:             )\n134:             # Post-Processing Column Swap Fallback (Python)\n135:             try:\n136:                 parsed = json.loads(response.text)\n137:                 items = parsed.get(\"items\", [])\n138:                 for item in items:\n139:                     qty = item.get('quantity', 0)\n140:                     rate = item.get('unit_rate', 0)\n141:                     total = item.get('total_amount', 0)\n142:                     \n143:                     # If total matches qty exactly and rate is small (e.g. qty=535, rate=2, total=535), \n144:                     # it means qty and rate were misaligned. Swap them:\n145:                     if total > 0 and qty == total and rate in [1, 2, 1.0, 2.0]:\n146:                         item['quantity'] = 1.0\n147:                         item['unit_rate'] = total\n148: \n149:                 sanitized = sanitize_invoice_data(parsed)\n150:                 return Response(content=json.dumps(sanitized), media_type=\"application/json\")\n151:             except Exception as e:\n152:                 print(f\"[AUDIT IT] Post-processing note: {e}\")\n153:                 return Response(content=response.text, media_type=\"application/json\")\n154:         except Exception as err:\n155:             last_err = err\n156:             err_str = str(err)\n157:             # If 404 not found (model retired by Google) or 503 spike, try next candidate\n158:             if \"404\" in err_str or \"503\" in err_str or \"not found\" in err_str.lower():\n159:                 print(f\"[AUDIT IT] Model {model_name} unavailable ({err_str[:80]}), trying next...\")\n160:                 continue"}
